# Manim build output. Only the final 1080p60 mp4s are tracked, because the site
# serves them; everything else here is regenerated by ./build-media.sh.
#
# These patterns were copied from the SPC repo, where `media/` sat at the repo
# root. Here it lives at `msa-lab/media/`, and a gitignore pattern containing a
# slash is anchored to the directory holding the file - so every rule below was
# dead from the first commit and 444 MB went in unnoticed: 6 wav files at 252 MB,
# 2447 Text-cache entries, 766 partial movies, 389 low-quality proofs. The `**/`
# prefix is what makes them match at any depth. A test in
# msa-lab/tests/test_page_claims.py now holds this.
**/media/videos/**/480p15/
**/media/videos/**/partial_movie_files/
**/media/videos/**/*.wav
**/media/videos/**/*.srt
**/media/voiceovers/
**/media/texts/
**/media/images/
**/media/Tex/
**/__pycache__/
**/.venv/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/node_modules/
